 "path": "task-notes/task-43165969.md",
 "content": "# Continual-ARC task 43165969 notes\n\nObserved rule pattern from 7 demonstrations (sizes varied): for each n×n input, output has size 2n×2n. The upper-left n×n block exactly equals the input. Remaining cells appear to be randomly generated using the input's color palette/distribution; no deterministic spatial transform was discernible from the examples. Examples: 5×5→10×10, 6×6→12×12, 7×7→14×14, 9×9→18×18, 11×11→22×22, 13×13→26×26. A monochrome all-8 input yields an all-8 output. In varied-color examples the added three quadrants look random; do not assume mirroring, rotation, tiling, or filling with background. Test was 8×8, so output dimensions should have been 16×16, and first 8×8 must match exactly. Submissions that duplicated input across quadrants or filled added region mostly with 8 were incorrect. The main unresolved possibility: the remaining cells are random draws based on input palette/frequencies, perhaps impossible to predict from demos absent a deterministic generator rule/seed."
